{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":496274,"duration_api_ms":567061,"ttft_ms":1673,"ttft_stream_ms":877,"time_to_request_ms":19,"num_turns":45,"result":"# Change Plan\n\n## Task Classification\n**Feature** (additive) — introduces a read cache with write-driven invalidation inside `server/storage/mvcc`; no existing contract is altered, only extended.\n\n## Affected Cells\n| Cell | Files to Modify | What Changes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `server/storage/mvcc` | `watchable_store.go`, `watchable_store_txn.go`, `kvstore.go` (StoreConfig only), new `watchable_store_range_cache.go`, `CODEMANIFEST` | Add bounded read cache + eviction hook + config default; document in manifest |\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\nNo caching exists anywhere in `server/storage/mvcc` today (confirmed by grep + full file reads). Both linearizable and serializable `Range` calls converge on one implementation (`rangeKeys`, `kvstore_txn.go:73-152`) reached via `KV.Range` → `readView.Range` → `store.Read` → `storeTxnCommon.Range`. All writes converge on one commit point: `watchableStoreTxnWrite.End()` (`watchable_store_txn.go:22-47`), which already holds `watchableStore.mu.Lock()` while computing the exact changed-key list (`evs`) and before delegating to `storeTxnWrite.End()` where `currentRev` is incremented (`kvstore_txn.go:214`, the sole mutation site). This single write choke point, combined with `watchableStore.mu`'s existing `RWMutex`, is sufficient to implement a race-free cache without any new synchronization primitive.\n\n## Trace Summary\n- Read: `KV.Range` (promoted from `store.ReadView`) → will be shadowed by new `watchableStore.Range` → cache check → miss falls through to today's exact `s.store.Range(...)` (unmodified `readView.Range` → `rangeKeys`).\n- Write: `writeView.Put/DeleteRange` → `watchableStore.Write` → `watchableStoreTxnWrite.End()` (existing `mu.Lock()` section) → **new**: evict overlapping cache entries → existing `notify(rev, evs)` → existing `TxnWrite.End()` (currentRev++).\n- Restore: `watchableStore.Restore` (existing `mu.Lock()` section) → **new**: clear cache entirely.\n\n## Change Strategy\n1. **`kvstore.go`**: add `ReadCacheSize int` to `StoreConfig`; add `defaultReadCacheSize = <N>` (e.g. 1024) alongside the existing `defaultCompactionBatchLimit`/`defaultCompactionSleepInterval`; in `NewStore`, if `cfg.ReadCacheSize == 0`, set it to the default — mirrors the existing zero-value-default idiom exactly, so all existing callers (who never set this field) get caching on by default with no code change required on their part.\n2. **New file `watchable_store_range_cache.go`**: define `rangeCacheKey{key, hasEnd, end string; limit int64; countOnly, fastKeysOnly, withTotalCount bool}` (a string/bool-only struct, safe as a map key) and `rangeCache{mu sync.Mutex; entries map[rangeCacheKey]*RangeResult; order []rangeCacheKey; maxEntries int}` with methods `get(k) (*RangeResult, bool)`, `put(k, *RangeResult)` (bounded FIFO eviction when `len(entries) >= maxEntries`), `invalidate(key, end []byte)` (removes every entry whose interval contains the given single changed key, using the same nil/empty/bounded semantics as `ReadView.Range`'s doc comment), and `clear()`. Pure data structure, no dependency on `store`/`watchableStore` — keeps it independently testable.\n3. **`watchable_store.go`**: add `cache *rangeCache` field to `watchableStore`; initialize in `newWatchableStore` via `newRangeCache(cfg.ReadCacheSize)`; in `Restore`, call `s.cache.clear()` inside the existing `s.mu.Lock()` section.\n4. **`watchable_store.go` (or new file)**: add\n   ```go\n   func (s *watchableStore) Range(ctx context.Context, key, end []byte, ro RangeOptions) (*RangeResult, error) {\n       if ro.Rev <= 0 {\n           if r, ok := s.cache.get(newRangeCacheKey(key, end, ro)); ok {\n               return r, nil\n           }\n       }\n       s.mu.RLock()\n       r, err := s.store.Range(ctx, key, end, ro)\n       if ro.Rev <= 0 && err == nil {\n           s.cache.put(newRangeCacheKey(key, end, ro), r)\n       }\n       s.mu.RUnlock()\n       return r, err\n   }\n   ```\n   This shadows the promoted `store.Range` (Go method resolution prefers the outer type's explicit method), so `KV.Range` on a `*watchableStore` now flows through here. `s.store.Range(...)` is the exact unmodified call used today — the miss path is byte-for-byte identical to current behavior.\n5. **`watchable_store_txn.go`**: inside `watchableStoreTxnWrite.End()`, after `evs` is built and before/alongside `tw.s.notify(rev, evs)` (same `tw.s.mu.Lock()` section, no new lock), add: for each `change := range changes { tw.s.cache.invalidate(change.Key, nil) }` — i.e., treat every changed key as a single-key invalidation probe against all cached ranges (a changed key always has a concrete key, never a range, so `end=nil` semantics apply to the *changed* side; the cached entry's own `[key,end)` shape determines containment).\n6. **CODEMANIFEST**: update the `KV()::Range` method annotation to describe the cache/invalidation contract at a behavioral level (no staleness beyond an uncached read; invalidation is write-driven, not timer-driven) and add a new `Usages` entry (e.g. `read_cache_invalidation`) explaining the `watchableStore.mu` ordering guarantee for anyone extending the write path later, referenced from both `Range` and the write-path annotations. This is finalized in the Manifest Reconciliation step but is scoped now so the implementer writes annotation-consistent code/comments.\n\n## Specification Impact\n- `KV()::Range` method annotation gains a documented caching/invalidation behavior clause (additive — does not change the existing \"read the current (or historical) value(s)\" contract, only clarifies that current-revision reads may be served from an internally-invalidated cache with no observable staleness).\n- New `Usages` entry documenting the `watchableStore.mu` happens-before argument, so future modifications to the write path preserve the invariant this cache depends on.\n- No signature, type, or location changes to any currently-documented entity (`KV`, `WatchableKV`, `TxnRead`, `TxnWrite`, `New`) — `StoreConfig`'s new field is not itself a documented body entity (only referenced as \"compaction batch size and pacing\" in `New`'s annotation), so its annotation text gets one clause added noting cache sizing, not a new entity block.\n\n## Usage Impact\n- `watch_sync_states` usage: no change required — invalidation reuses its existing lock/hook point without altering synced/unsynced/victim semantics; worth a one-line cross-reference addition in the new `read_cache_invalidation` usage (\"piggybacks on the same `End()` critical section documented in `watch_sync_states`\") for discoverability, not a behavioral edit.\n- No consumer-facing `.usages/` recipes exist yet for this cell's external consumers to update (none found in scope resolution); if a cell-level `.usages/` directory is later added for `server/storage/mvcc` consumers, it's out of scope for this change.\n\n## Compatibility Verification\n**Backward compatible.** All existing exported signatures (`KV`, `WatchableKV`, `ReadView.Range`, `WriteView.Put/DeleteRange`, `TxnRead`, `TxnWrite`, `New`, `NewStore`) are unchanged. `StoreConfig` gains one new field with a zero-value-safe default (existing struct literals using positional-free field names, i.e. `StoreConfig{CompactionBatchLimit: x, CompactionSleepInterval: y}`, are unaffected; any exceedingly rare positional literal `StoreConfig{x, y}` would fail to compile if a new field is inserted between existing ones — **mitigation**: append `ReadCacheSize` as the last field to avoid any positional-literal risk). Miss-path behavior is a direct passthrough to the current implementation. Hit-path behavior is proven equivalent to what an uncached call would return at the same logical instant (Investigation Report §\"Confirmed Root Cause\"). No test relying on \"identical repeated Range calls independently re-scan the backend\" is expected to exist (that's an implementation detail, not documented behavior) — will be confirmed empirically in Testing.\n\n## Test Strategy\n1. **Unit — `rangeCache`** (new `watchable_store_range_cache_test.go`): get/put/miss, FIFO eviction at `maxEntries`, `invalidate` containment logic for all three end-semantics (single key, from-key, bounded range), `clear`.\n2. **Integration — `watchableStore`** (extend `watchable_store_test.go` or new `watchable_store_range_cache_integration_test.go`):\n   - Repeated identical `Range` (ro.Rev=0) returns identical result without a second backend scan (assert via a counting/instrumented backend or by asserting result pointer/content equality plus a call-counter hook).\n   - `Put` on a cached key is visible on the very next `Range` call (no staleness) — race-focused test issuing `Range` concurrently with `Put` across many iterations (`go test -race -count=N`) to empirically stress the ordering proof.\n   - `Range` with `ro.Rev` explicitly pinned (> 0) is never cached / always reflects fresh reads (including after compaction), i.e. unaffected by this change.\n   - `DeleteRange` and lease-expiry-driven deletes (via `SetRangeDeleter`) invalidate correctly.\n   - `Restore` clears the cache.\n   - Cache correctness under `-race`.\n3. **Existing test suite**: run full `server/storage/mvcc` test suite (`kvstore_test.go`, `watchable_store_test.go`, `watcher_test.go`, etc.) unmodified to confirm no regression, plus relevant `server/etcdserver` integration tests exercising `Range` (linearizable and serializable).\n\n## Risk Assessment\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Missed invalidation path (e.g. a future write entry point bypassing `watchableStoreTxnWrite.End()`) | Low | High (silent staleness) | Confined to `watchableStore.Write()` being the sole `WriteView` construction point for the production KV (verified: `writeView.kv` is always the `*watchableStore`); new `Usages` entry documents the invariant for future maintainers |\n| Increased lock contention on `watchableStore.mu` from every cache-miss read now taking `RLock()` | Medium | Low-Medium (perf, not correctness) | `RWMutex` readers don't block each other; only excluded by writers' brief `Lock()` during `End()`; cache hits (the optimized hot path) take no lock at all |\n| Unbounded memory growth from high-cardinality distinct query shapes | Low (bounded by config) | Medium | `ReadCacheSize` bounds entry count with FIFO eviction; default sized conservatively |\n| `StoreConfig` field insertion breaking positional struct literals | Low | Low (compile-time, not runtime) | New field appended last; grep codebase for positional `StoreConfig{...}` literals during implementation to confirm zero occurrences |\n| Race between compaction and cache (return stale historical data) | None (by design) | N/A | Caching strictly excluded for `ro.Rev > 0`; compaction never affects current-revision values |\n| Cache logic itself introduces a data race (map access) | Low | High if present | `rangeCache` uses its own `sync.Mutex`; will be validated under `go test -race` |\n\n---\n\nDo you approve the plan? Proceed to implementation?","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"383754f8-4778-4194-a29a-4b501ed4b48e","total_cost_usd":2.5935807000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":56,"cache_creation_input_tokens":148639,"cache_read_input_tokens":2019758,"output_tokens":45980,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":148639,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":70,"outputTokens":53713,"cacheReadInputTokens":2286089,"cacheCreationInputTokens":204643,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.5935807000000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"c